     "text": "FAX 4  CONFIDENTIAL\n**Coleman-Williams Medical Group**\n\n**Dear Colleague,**\n\nI had the pleasure of consulting with Brittany Howard on February 26, 2025. This visit was prompted by concerns regarding her hypothyroidism. Here are the details of our discussion and the current status of her medical conditions:\n\n**Medical History:**\n\n**Gout:**\nBrittany was diagnosed with gout on October 20, 2024. her condition is currently well-controlled. She is taking allopurinol 100 mg daily, which has been effective in managing her gout symptoms. During this visit, she reported no recent episodes of gout flares. Her blood pressure was 114/71 mmHg, and she weighed 126 pounds.\n\n**Hypothyroidism:**\nBrittany has been managing hypothyroidism since December 2, 2018. She is currently on levothyroxine 25 mcg daily, and her thyroid function tests have remained within the range. She reports no symptoms of hypothyroidism such as fatigue, cold intolerance, or weight gain. During this visit, her physical exam was unremarkable with no palpable thyroid enlargement or tenderness.\n\n**Physical Exam:**\nThe physical examination was generally unremarkable. Her cardiovascular and respiratory examinations were normal with no abnormalities detected. Her thyroid gland was not enlarged, and there were no signs of hyperthyroidism or hypothyroidism on physical exam. Her joints, particularly those previously affected by gout, showed no signs of inflammation or deformity.\n\n**Impression and Recommendations:**\nBased on the current status of her conditions, I believe Brittany is effectively managing her gout and hypothyroidism with her current medications. There is no indication to change her current treatment plan. She should continue with her current dosage of allopurinol and levothyroxine. I recommend she maintains regular follow-ups to monitor her conditions and adjust her medications if necessary.\n\n**Social History:**\nBrittany is a former smoker who quit smoking on December 13, 2006, after a 21-year habit of smoking half a pack per day. She consumes alcohol occasionally, averaging about one drink per week. Her family history is significant for Alzheimer's disease in father, who is currently 70 years old and living.\n\n**Summary:**\nBrittany Howard is currently managing her gout and hypothyroidism well with appropriate medications. Her physical examination was normal, and she reports no symptoms related to her conditions. I appreciate the referral and look forward to continuing her care.\n\n**Sincerely,**\n\n**Dr. Richard Guerrero** \n**Family Medicine Specialist** \n**Coleman-Williams Medical Group**\n"
